    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "What an OS does",
     "md": "An **operating system (OS)** manages the hardware and runs the other programs. Main functions: **memory management**, **file management**, **managing input/output devices**, **multitasking** (running several programs), **security** (user accounts and passwords) and providing a **user interface**."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "User interfaces",
     "md": "A **GUI** (graphical user interface) uses windows, icons, menus and a pointer; it is easy for beginners. A **command-line interface (CLI)** uses typed commands; it is fast for experts but harder to learn. Examples of OS: Windows, Linux, macOS, Android."
    },
