     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Files and folders",
     "md": "A **file** holds data and has a name and an **extension** that shows its type (.docx document, .xlsx spreadsheet, .jpg image, .mp3 sound, .txt plain text). A **folder** (directory) groups files. A **path** like Documents/School/Maths.docx shows where a file is stored."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- Deleting a file in a folder does not always delete it permanently (the recycle bin may keep it).\n- Changing a file extension does not change the file's real content.\n- Closing a window is not the same as shutting down the computer: always use shut down."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1 - Extensions",
     "statement": "Name the type of file for budget.xlsx, song.mp3 and notes.txt.",
     "steps": [
      "budget.xlsx: the extension .xlsx is a spreadsheet.",
      "song.mp3: sound; notes.txt: plain text."
     ],
     "answer": "Spreadsheet, sound, plain text."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2 - Path",
     "statement": "A file Report.docx is in the folder Term1, inside the folder School, inside Documents. Write its path.",
     "steps": [
      "Start from the outer folder and go inward: Documents, then School, then Term1.",
      "Add the file name at the end."
     ],
     "answer": "Documents/School/Term1/Report.docx"
    }
