    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Cells and formulas",
     "md": "A spreadsheet is a grid of **columns** (A, B, C...) and **rows** (1, 2, 3...). A **cell** is named by its column and row, e.g. B3. A **formula** starts with = and calculates a value, e.g. =B2\\*C2. When a cell changes, formulas update automatically."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Common functions",
     "md": "=SUM(B2:B6) adds the range B2 to B6. =AVERAGE(B2:B6) gives the mean. =MAX() and =MIN() give the largest and smallest. =COUNT() counts numbers. =IF(B2>=50,\"Pass\",\"Fail\") chooses between two results."
    },
