    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Word processing",
     "md": "A **word processor** creates and edits documents. Features: **formatting** (font, size, bold, alignment), **editing** (copy, cut, paste, find and replace), page layout (margins, columns, page numbers), tables, **spell check**, headers/footers and mail merge (sending the same letter to many people)."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Database basics",
     "md": "A **database** is an organised collection of data. A **table** has **fields** (columns, e.g. Name) and **records** (rows, one per person or item). A **primary key** is a field whose value is unique for each record (e.g. a student ID)."
